{
  "skill": "otel-audit",
  "prompts": [
    {
      "id": "agent-resource-table-audit",
      "eval_inputs": [
        "eval/inputs/agent-resource-cases.json"
      ],
      "task": "Use $otel-audit ./service. Also assess each independent source case in eval/inputs/agent-resource-cases.json and save a supplemental .observe/agent-resource-cases.json with its source-owned role, producer/destination choice, project/stream/routing assessment and remaining proof. Keep the actual service canonical audit and HTML distinct from those source cases. Remain read-only for application source, configuration, dependencies and tests; no models, cloud, resource provisioning, browser or UI actions. Do not reuse old classifications without inspecting source. No resource names, library choices or destination changes are supplied by this request. Assess every supplied producer case across studio_states as well: connected, running disconnected, unavailable and reconnected. Separate proposed capability from actual proof. Galileo/direct destinations remain independent. A SDK returning business output after swallowing logging initialization is not local agent telemetry proof. Also assess native_startup_cases independently: define a distinct new-process acceptance case for the prevalidated persisted binding with its resource API unavailable and local OTLP receiver available. Keep it separate from same-PID names-only activation and distinguish retained routing from fresh resource-resolution evidence. Before finalizing supplemental cases, execute a source-ledger consistency check on all proposed operation/parent/field/lifecycle rows and save its outcome. A report-only negative control must insert an agent-with-model/tool-children lifecycle into the single-inference non-agent case and be rejected; do not change the actual source or canonical classifications. Include current versus proposed provider/exporter/destination ownership in the same ledger and routing/profile consistency check. A second report-only negative must claim an existing HTTP exporter for the fresh Go source with no telemetry setup and be rejected. Propose new selected native or SDK setup where none exists; unselected alternatives remain explicitly conditional, not claims of current topology. Bind every routing required_fix/API signature to its case language, not only the provider table. A report-only negative that pastes Python SpanExporter.export/ReadableSpan into the selected Go routing fix must be rejected or explicitly marked unsupported. Include the complete shared names-only acceptance: request-time and retry-rate/backoff bounds, local/business progress and shutdown cancellation, with source-unavailable settings stated as gaps rather than invented. Distinguish SDK span creation from transport: the documented supported helper on a registered native OTel provider remains an SDK path, while manual native creator replacement needs its exact per-operation exception. Include a destination-scoped report-only negative control: insert the Studio names-only UUID trace-header/Resource activation acceptance into a Galileo-native routing row (or an inherited shared scenario) while leaving its provider/required_fix correct. The consistency check must reject that destination mismatch. Preserve native Galileo resources, configured production stream and the separate operator OTLP sink."
    }
  ],
  "judge_inputs": [
    "Inspect original actual app source, each independent source case, canonical audit/HTML, supplemental JSON and actor commands. Merely repeating a policy table is not source-bound assessment."
  ],
